## What #4471 holds

<SplitTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

## How each report is placed

A report is placed by its tenant and the way it came in, and by what its body says. The intake
tag is a guess from the reporter's browser, so this page does not use it.

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first, and these tenants write the day
  first. Day and month swap: a booking for 7 April goes out as 4 July. It covers app and email
  reports from every day-first tenant, and form reports from tenants on booking-v2, whose hint
  already says `DD/MM/YYYY`.
- **`hint`**: the booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. Customers of a
  day-first tenant follow the hint, and the form reads what they typed the tenant's way. This
  covers reports that came in through the form of a tenant on booking-v3. The parser fix does not
  touch it, because the form receives the wrong input.
- **`clock`**: the booking moves by exactly one day, with day and month in the right place. The
  desk read these bodies as a one-day move and listed them in its notes. One customer in Lisbon
  and one in Toronto saw different days for the same meeting, so this is a time zone problem. The
  desk filed these reports under `parser` by tenant, and the parser fix does not touch them either.

## What to do on the desk

- Do not merge a new date report into #4471 on subject alone. Place it with the
  [triage explorer](/kb/triage/dedupe) first, then merge it into the ticket for its problem.
- When a body describes a one-day move, add its id to the desk notes, so the table above counts it
  under `clock`.
- Keep #4471 open until the tickets for all three problems are closed.

